SELECT '2c6afad5-83b8-5197-a9e4-0cbaae09442c'::uuid, 'JF Effect | Physique Specialization — Advanced — 4 days/week', 'block', 'bodybuilding', 'Hypertrophy', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'Men', 'Muscle', 'Hypertrophy', 'Advanced', 'Gym', '4 days', 'Upper Lower']::text[], 'Published', 12, 4,
  75, 'Advanced hypertrophy with emphasis on lats, delts, upper chest and arms', $jf$Advanced bodybuilding, 4 days a week. Fewer, better sets after proper warm-ups: a handful of hard working sets per muscle, close to failure on the stable machine and cable work, with emphasis on the lats, side delts, upper chest and arms. Optional rest-pause on the last isolation set in the hardest weeks. Not a failure-every-set program and not six days in the gym. About 60–85 minutes.$jf$, $jf$Purpose: high-quality hypertrophy with emphasis options for lats, side/rear delts, upper chest and arms. Dorian Yates-inspired execution: fewer, excellent working sets after warm-ups; no compulsory failure or forced reps.
Weekly sets (approx.): back 11, chest 8, side delts 6, rear delts 2, quads 10, hamstrings 6, glutes 2 + compounds, calves 4, biceps 4, triceps 2 + pressing.
Specialization: pick 1–2 lagging muscles and move 2–4 weekly hard sets from non-priority work to them (e.g. +1 lateral raise set each upper day, −1 leg extension and −1 seated calf). Never 3+ redundant rows/pulldowns in one day.
Intensity techniques: optional rest-pause on the final set of a safe isolation (machines/cables) in Weeks 7, 10 and 11 only.
Trim first if over 85 min: cable crunch, seated calf raise, then one set of the hammer curl.
Changes from the JF Effect master spec (Nov 13 2026), and why:
- Chest was 4 hard sets a week for an advanced physique program that lists upper chest as an emphasis. The incline press and machine chest press go from 2 to 3 sets, and Upper B's dumbbell shoulder press becomes a pec deck (2x10–15): front delts already get 6 hard pressing sets, side delts get 6 lateral-raise sets, and the press added joint stress without new stimulus. Chest goes to 8 sets a week.$jf$,
