SELECT '7dcc2281-fcf3-51ac-ae3f-6cfcb559ea6a'::uuid, 'JF Effect | Fitness Foundation — Beginner — 3 days/week', 'block', 'lifestyle', 'Hypertrophy', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'Women', 'Glutes', 'Strength', 'Beginner', 'Gym', '3 days', 'Full Body']::text[], 'Published', 12, 3,
  55, 'Full-body strength and confidence with real glute and leg work', $jf$Three full-body workouts a week to build strength and confidence in the gym, with proper glute and leg work and a balanced upper body. Real weights, not light ones: you add weight whenever you hit the top of the rep range. Machines and dumbbells that are easy to learn, an easier week every fourth week, and a rep-PR week at the end. About 45–60 minutes. Optional: 2 easy 15–30 minute walks or bike rides a week.$jf$, $jf$Purpose: full-body strength and confidence with meaningful glute/lower-body work. Not 'light weights because female'.
Weekly sets (approx.): quads 9, glutes 5 direct + compounds, hamstrings 4, back 7, chest 4, delts 4, core 2 exercises.
Double progression at the target RIR. Weeks 4 and 8 are lighter weeks (same movements, 3-set work drops a set, 3–4 RIR).
Scale exercise choice to skill and joints: goblet squat or belt squat, split squat with or without dumbbells. For a true novice, drop one set from the hip thrust and leg press in Block 1.
Trim first if over 60 min: plank or dead bug, then the lateral raise.$jf$,
