SELECT 'f75d80f5-2a09-562a-9c9c-bbdbb55b9261'::uuid, 'JF Effect | Advanced Physique — Advanced — 4 days/week', 'block', 'bodybuilding', 'Hypertrophy', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'Women', 'Glutes', 'Hypertrophy', 'Advanced', 'Gym', '4 days', 'Upper Lower']::text[], 'Published', 12, 4,
  70, 'Glute and leg specialization with quality upper-body development', $jf$For experienced lifters building glutes and legs without neglecting the upper body. A heavy hip thrust top set with back-off sets, Romanian deadlifts, split squats, step-ups and a heavy squat, plus two upper days for back, shoulders, chest and arms. Precise, not just more: every set has a job. About 60–80 minutes, 4 days a week.$jf$, $jf$Purpose: glute/leg specialization with quality upper-body work. Higher precision, not automatically higher volume.
Hip thrust: top set 6–8 (5–7 in Block 3) at 1–2 RIR, then 2 back-offs at 92% of the top set (skip the drop if the bar can't be loaded that finely).
Weekly sets (approx.): glutes 3–5 direct + abduction 4 + compounds; hamstrings 6; quads 9; back 8; delts 8 (lateral 3, rear 3, press 2); chest 4; arms 2+2.
Pick 1–2 specialization muscles and shift sets toward them; preserve the upper body. The optional glute bridge on Day 4 is only for weeks when performance and recovery are good.
Intensity techniques: optional rest-pause on the final set of safe isolations in Weeks 7, 10, 11.
Trim first if over 80 min: optional glute bridge, then one set of the reverse pec deck.$jf$,
