SELECT '0d6dc03d-cd4f-5ab1-9e53-f1cfeda2232e'::uuid, 'JF Effect | Bodyweight Foundation — Bodyweight only — 3 days/week', 'block', 'lifestyle', 'Technique', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'At Home', 'Home', 'Bodyweight', 'Full Body', '3 days', 'Any level']::text[], 'Published', 12, 3,
  40, 'Practical strength and fitness at home with no equipment', $jf$Three full-body workouts at home with zero equipment: no bench, bar or bands. Squats, lunges, push-ups, bridges and core work, made harder over 12 weeks with slower reps, pauses, harder variations and single-leg work instead of weights. Every exercise has an easier and a harder version so it fits your level. One honest limit: with no equipment there's no real pulling exercise, so your back gets upper-back drills, not rows. If you later get a pull-up bar or bands, ask your coach for the upgrade. About 30–45 minutes.$jf$, $jf$Purpose: practical strength/fitness starting point with zero equipment, scaled to ability by exercise variation.
Equipment: none assumed (no pull-up bar, bench, bands, chair or door anchor). Never prescribe door-frame, furniture or towel-anchor rows as defaults.
Limitation (disclosed to the client): prone W / Y-T-W / reverse snow angels are upper-back health drills, not a substitute for rows or pulldowns. Upgrade path if they get a pull-up bar or bands: add rows/pull-downs and move the prone drills to warm-ups.
Progression order: cleaner range and control → more reps → harder leverage or single-leg variation → one more set only when justified. Push-up path: incline/knees → full → 3-second lowering → pause at the bottom → pike push-ups (Day 2) once 15 clean push-ups are easy.
Optional if they have a smooth floor and a towel: sliding leg curls for hamstrings (not assumed).
Changes from the JF Effect master spec (Nov 13 2026), and why:
- Push-ups use one library exercise all week with a different emphasis each day (standard, 3-second lowering, pause at the bottom) instead of switching to pike push-ups by default: most people starting with zero equipment can't do a safe pike push-up yet; it's the Day 2 progression once 15 push-ups are easy.$jf$,
