SELECT '9ef5e4b4-ac6f-5fad-b51f-d3390cc999e9'::uuid, 'JF Effect | Dumbbell Muscle Builder — Dumbbells only — 3 days/week', 'block', 'bodybuilding', 'Hypertrophy', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'At Home', 'Home', 'Dumbbells', 'Muscle', 'Full Body', '3 days', 'Any level']::text[], 'Published', 12, 3,
  50, 'Build muscle and strength at home with one pair of adjustable dumbbells', $jf$Full-body muscle building with one pair of adjustable dumbbells and some floor space: no bench, cables, bands or pull-up bar. Every press is done on the floor and every row is done standing. When the dumbbells get too light, you progress with reps, single-leg work and slower lowering instead of junk sets. About 40–55 minutes, 3 days a week.$jf$, $jf$Equipment: adjustable dumbbells + floor (~10x10 ft). No bench, bands, cables, machines, pull-up bar or door attachment assumed. Benches/bands only as clearly optional swaps once confirmed.
Weekly sets (approx.): quads 9, hamstrings 5, glutes 2 + compounds, chest 6, back 6 + rear delts 2, delts 3 + 2, arms 2 + 2.
If the dumbbells are too light for bilateral legs, move to split-stance/unilateral work and higher controlled reps rather than adding sets. Adjust set counts to the load range they actually own.
Double progression; smallest dumbbell jump available. When there's no heavier dumbbell: more reps, slower lowering, a pause, single-leg/arm, then an extra set only if recovery allows. No endless tempo tricks.$jf$,
