SELECT '967ca531-3098-5501-b3b7-9c2c571d2c4c'::uuid, 'JF Effect | At-Home Physique Builder — Dumbbells + bodyweight — 4 days/week', 'block', 'bodybuilding', 'Hypertrophy', ARRAY['JF Effect', 'At Home', 'Home', 'Dumbbells', 'Muscle', 'Upper Lower', '4 days', 'Any level']::text[], 'Published', 12, 4,
  55, 'Upper/lower muscle building at home without machines, a bench or cables', $jf$Upper/lower muscle building at home: two lower and two upper days with dumbbells and your bodyweight. No machines, bench or cables, and every exercise fits a small space. Floor presses, standing rows, split squats, Romanian deadlifts and push-ups, made harder over 12 weeks with small weight jumps, reps and single-leg work. About 45–60 minutes, 4 days a week.$jf$, $jf$Equipment: adjustable dumbbells + bodyweight + floor. No bench, multiple stations or improvised supports. A dumbbell + bodyweight superset (e.g. floor press with push-ups) only if it saves time without costing hard sets.
Weekly sets (approx.): quads 10, hamstrings 5, glutes 4 + compounds, chest 8, back 6 + rear delts 2, delts 2 + 2, biceps 4, triceps 2 + pressing, calves 2.
Progress with the smallest dumbbell jump, then reps, unilateral leverage and range. Not endless tempo tricks.
Scale every exercise to the person's actual skill: this program is equipment-gated, not experience-gated.
Changes from the JF Effect master spec (Nov 13 2026), and why:
- Upper B: the optional prone W raise is replaced by a dumbbell hammer curl (2x10–15). With dumbbells available, rows and rear-delt raises already load the upper back properly, and biceps had only 2 direct sets a week in an intermediate/advanced physique program.
- Upper B: the spec's 'dumbbell squeeze floor press' uses the library's floor press with a squeeze cue (press the dumbbells together the whole rep) instead of creating a near-duplicate exercise.$jf$,
